// Consumer: directory-derived recurring_failure_mode.roster, projected by
// gunbc.design_ledgers.expected_design_failure_modes_md through docs_projection_gate.
data empty_list_evaluates_to_unit: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "empty_list_evaluates_to_unit" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: an empty list used as a value evaluates as kernel Unit. v1_interpreter.eval_expr_inner on ExprData::NoExprData returned Value::Unit. A List/Set type node (make_container_type) and an empty literal whose typed node lost ExprListLit are NoExprData. concat then pushed that Unit into the result list, so a later field read names Unit as the runtime carrier.",

    "SPECIMEN, executed 2026-10-08 on gunbc#13475 generated job 113113331249 at f2106c2cd: `cannot access field 'path' on Unit` at dag/extdeps/deepseek/deepseek_v4_1_flash.dag published_file_identity_line <- published_file_identity_eq <- list_member <- deepseek_v4_1_flash_admit_tokenizer_population. The producer is fold(..., init: [] as List<DeepseekV41PublishedFile>, concat(acc, [f])). Same class: roadmap_emit cannot access field tbuf on Unit; host-sudoers cannot cast NonEmptyStr (runtime carrier Unit) to String. The checker had already typed the accumulator as a list; the seed evaluator did not inhabit that type.",

    "HARM: fabricated plausible output at eval (DESIGN section 5). The program is Accepted and then the wet/generated lanes refuse on a type the program never had. Neighbouring class unsolved_placeholder_reads_back_as_unit is checker diagnostic fabrication; this class is the evaluator substituting Unit for an empty collection.",

    "PRODUCER: v1_interpreter.eval_expr_inner NoExprData arm returned Unit; concat then pushed that Unit as an element (free_monoid_to_vec had no empty-Unit flatten).",

    "CLIMB, gunbc#13475: NoExprData whose inferred (or self) node is an element collection evaluates as the empty list. Concat does not treat a leftover Unit as empty (review 77857: that flatten is an absorbing fallback). child_type_node keeps a TypeVariable child so the type node is not collapsed to error_type/Unit before eval. Admitted under gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing v1_seed_standing: seed defect that silently produced a wrong value, serving the v2 corpus the seed compiles.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable (loud TypeError at eval). CLIMBED ON #13475 to mechanically preventable for the empty-collection-as-Unit arm. CEILING: 4 -- an empty list has no constructor that is Unit. NEXT TRIGGER: empty-list literals keep ExprListLit through typing so NoExprData is not the empty-list value path.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
